# ioctl-codex — sepolicy.rule
#
# The module is designed to need NO custom SELinux policy:
#   * the Zygisk loader (root/zygote context) reads /data/adb/ioctl-codex,
#   * the menu .so is staged into the app's own data dir, which the app may
#     already read+execute under untrusted_app / priv_app,
#   * the only privileged action (moving a finished dump to /sdcard) goes
#     through the Zygisk root companion, which runs in the module's context.
#
# A malformed sepolicy.rule can prevent boot, so we intentionally ship none.
# If a particular device still denies the /sdcard move, the fix is to add a
# rule for the target domain (untrusted_app_27..35) permitting
#   allow <domain> media_rw_data_file:dir { create write };
# but that is device- and ROM-specific and is left to the user's judgement.
